    54	J(p,r)= 3y^2 T T_x,
    55	J(q,r)= 6y   T T_x.
    56	```
    57	
    58	All three are nonzero. They are therefore the leading forms of the
    59	actual three Jacobian minors after restriction, whose exact degrees are
    60	
