+  =(J(G_1,G_2) after alpha) J(alpha_1,alpha_2).
+```
+
+If `beta` is the polynomial inverse of `alpha`, applying the chain rule to
+`beta after alpha=id` shows that `J(alpha_1,alpha_2)` is a unit of `k[x,y]`,
